                        "entry_id": "7e6d774b-3714-33f6-b446-85fd9ae4257e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To make not extinct; especially, to return an extinct species to existence."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1db7c3a7-d97d-4118-9b5b-5d45d51d6757",
                                "sense_id": "63d1b3a2-b5da-3d13-a69a-4c4c1fac91aa",
                                "text": "Removing graffiti.\nUnextincting the dodo bird."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "99bcad04-b8e4-450d-be32-87c52d7423ac",
                                "sense_id": "63d1b3a2-b5da-3d13-a69a-4c4c1fac91aa",
                                "text": "He was a resequenced neanderthal named Stiggins and soon to be, I assumed, divisional head of SO-13, the department that policed all unextincted creatures."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b2e6f816-2b6d-42fc-bc18-7dc14e596840",
                                "sense_id": "63d1b3a2-b5da-3d13-a69a-4c4c1fac91aa",
                                "text": "The good news is that, with the exception of the giant auk which will only return if genetic cloning can find a way to 'unextinct' it, there are ways of getting our wildlife out of the intensive care unit."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
